Title: DUST, BLOOD, AND GOLD: THE THREE COFFINS
Genre: Spaghetti Western
Recommended Style: Classic Pencil & Charcoal / Golden Age Hollywood

EXT. SAN PEDRO CEMETERY - HIGH NOON
[STYLE: Classic Pencil & Charcoal | CAMERA: Sergio Leone 3-Way Circular Standoff]

Harsh, blinding desert sunlight. Heat waves shimmer off weathered wooden grave crosses. A lone vulture circles lazily overhead.

THREE MEN stand in a triangular standoff fifty paces apart in the circular clearing:

1. THE STRANGER (poncho, unlit cigarillo clamped in teeth, hand hovering over his Colt revolver).
2. COLONEL CORTEZ (Confederate cavalry coat, saber scar across jaw, twin Remington pistols).
3. EL DIABLO (sombrero, bandoliers of dynamite, cruel calculating grin).

[SERGIO LEONE RAPID EDITING SEQUENCE]
- Extreme Close-Up: The Stranger's steel-blue squint.
- Extreme Close-Up: Cortez's sweating hand twitching above his holster.
- Extreme Close-Up: El Diablo's gold tooth glinting in the sun.
- Extreme Close-Up: The Stranger's fingers curling over the wooden revolver grip.

WIND HOWLS. A rusted graveyard bell tolls ONCE.

DRAW!
